From a973735a796759969629aa38b7234508b2760e52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 11:52:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(skills): render offline with vendored GSAP; catch
 unreadable text roles early
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two failures found driving faceless-explainer through two full films.

**Renders die when the GSAP CDN is unreachable.** Every workflow assembler and
captions.mjs hardcoded a jsdelivr URL, so on a machine behind an egress proxy,
in CI without outbound access, or offline, the page loads, `gsap` is never
defined, and every sub-composition registration throws. The render fails as
`sub_timeline_script_failure` naming a timeline rather than the network, and
only after the full frame capture has been paid for. Vendoring GSAP into the
project by hand did not survive, because re-assembly rewrote the CDN tag back.

lib/gsap-tag.mjs now picks the source: a project-vendored copy at
assets/vendor/ or public/vendor/ when one exists, else the pinned CDN build.
A vendored tag carries no integrity or crossorigin — those describe a
cross-origin fetch, and a hash pinned to the CDN build blocks a local file
outright, which is its own hard-to-read render failure. The assembler summary
now names which source it linked. Projects with nothing vendored behave exactly
as before. talking-head-recut already staged a local GSAP this way; this brings
the other four workflows in line.

**build-frame's self-check passed body copy at 2.65:1.** It compared only ink
against canvas, but a brand remix repaints roles by position and can land a
light accent in a text role — here #F97A4D into `text-muted` on white. Ink and
canvas still separated, so the check printed "contrast ok" and the failure
surfaced at the render-time contrast gate, after nine frames had been built
against the bad spec.

The self-check now reads the color roles the typography ramp actually paints
text with and measures each against the canvas at the same 3:1 floor the render
gate enforces, naming every failing role and its ratio. It reports rather than
dies, so a deliberate edge palette is not blocked. This needed a real WCAG
ratio: the existing lum() is a weighted sum of raw channels, which rates
orange-on-white far more readable than it is, so relLuminance()/contrastRatio()
are added alongside it rather than replacing it.

Both are covered by tests, including the 2.65:1 case as a regression. The
existing 596 skill tests still pass, captions.mjs stays byte-identical across
its three workflows, and the skill mirror check is clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
